  m_Name: 5_SurvivalOutsideHost
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Title: 'Survival Outside Host:'
  Description: M. tuberculosis can survive for months on dry inanimate surfaces. Tuberculosis
    can survive in cockroach faeces for 8 weeks, sputum on carpet (19 days) and wood
    (over 88 days), moist and dry soil (4 weeks), and in the environment for more
    than 74 days if protected from light (possibly longer if in faeces).
